                                        "entry_id": "7623bbb5-c41b-3717-ac72-59b49ac5d14d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A temporary shelter, often in the form of a tent, shed, or canopied structure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e2891df-83c7-43b1-ab76-fb1f67f92027",
                                                "sense_id": "4a1d21a2-04d6-3c3b-ba2e-14a2133ead1c",
                                                "text": "When Gro came to the Witches’ booths he found them guarded even as the Red Foliot had said, and the booths of them of Demonland in like manner. So went he into the royal booth where the King lay in state on a bier of spear-shafts, robed in his kingly robes over his armour that was painted black and inlaid with gold, and the crown of Witchland on his head."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e93a49a-7659-303d-be13-7f5874a46d48",
                                        "entry_id": "7623bbb5-c41b-3717-ac72-59b49ac5d14d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A boxlike room or enclosure just big enough to accommodate one standing person, such as a phone booth or polling booth."
                                        ],
